Shutdown Timer plugin
=====================

Lets a paired device schedule, inspect and cancel a delayed power action
(shut down, reboot or suspend) on this device, and lets this device do the
same on the paired device.

The timer is owned by the KDE Connect daemon of the device that will perform
the action: scheduling does not call into OS-level facilities (shutdown.exe,
"shutdown +30", ...) until the timer expires, which keeps the behaviour
identical on all supported platforms and makes the timer readable and
cancellable at any time.

Protocol
--------

kdeconnect.shutdowntimer (status, sent by the device that owns the timer):
    isActive (bool)   whether a timer is currently pending
    action   (string) "shutdown" | "reboot" | "suspend"; only when isActive
    deadline (long)   when the action fires, in msecs since epoch (UTC);
                      only when isActive. Receivers derive the remaining
                      time locally, so no periodic updates are sent.

It is sent when the local timer changes for any reason, when the peer asks
for it via requestStatus, and once on connect.

kdeconnect.shutdowntimer.request (control, sent by the controlling device):
    requestStatus (bool)   ask the peer to broadcast its current status
    cancel        (bool)   abort the pending timer, if any
    setAction     (string) + setSeconds (long)
                           schedule an action in the given number of seconds,
                           replacing any pending timer

Actions that the receiving platform cannot perform are rejected; the
unchanged status broadcast that follows acts as the negative acknowledgement.
